<title>FRANCE: NYK top destination Jan-Sept ex-Paris air exports.</title>
<headline>NYK top destination Jan-Sept ex-Paris air exports.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Paris airports authority, the Aeroports de Paris (ADP), said New York was the top destination for exports traffic from Charles de Gaulle and Orly Airports in the first nine months of 1996.</p>
<p>January-September 1996 Paris-New York air cargo volume totalled 28,947 tonnes, down 17.5 percent on the same period last year, ADP figures showed.</p>
<p>In second place, was Chicago, with 20,593 tonnes, up 14.6 percent on the first nine months of 1995.</p>
<p>Tokyo was ranked third with 19,999 tonnes flown from Paris in the period in question, a fall of seven percent on 1995 levels, ADP said.</p>
<p>The top ten destinations for ADP exports between January and September 1996 and the percentage change on the same period in 1995, were as follows:</p>
<p>    City		Tonnes	    Pct change from</p>
<p>						a year ago</p>
<p> 1  New York	  28,947 tonnes   -17.5pct</p>
<p> 2  Chicago	   20,593 tonnes   +14.6</p>
<p> 3  Tokyo	     19,999 tonnes    -7.0</p>
<p> 4  Hong Kong	 17,687 tonnes    -1.2</p>
<p> 5  Montreal	   8,699 tonnes   -20.8</p>
<p> 6  Mexico City	8,697 tonnes   +31.8</p>
<p> 7  Los Angeles	8,781 tonnes    +3.1</p>
<p> 8  Sao Paulo	  8,705 tonnes   -14.3</p>
<p> 9  Dubai		7,265 tonnes    -3.3</p>
<p> 10 Miami		6,802 tonnes  +108.4</p>
<p>- Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
</text>
